            <ArticleTitle>Ectopic molar near the coronoid process: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>597-600</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reports a case of retrieval of an ectopic molar medial to the coronoid process of the mandible that caused chronic discharging of a sinus into the mouth and recurrent facial swelling. Possible origin of the tooth and surgical approaches are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
